# Response headers, applied by Cloudflare to every static asset. The Content
# Security Policy proper is the `<meta>` Astro writes into each page with the
# hashes of what that page runs (`security.csp` in astro.config.mjs); the policy
# here only adds what a `<meta>` cannot carry. A response with two policies
# must satisfy both.
#
# Framing: only the author's portfolio (dennisgr7.dev) may show the page in a
# frame, as the live preview on its Snob CLI entry
# (src/scripts/portfolio-preview.ts). There is no X-Frame-Options: it cannot
# name an origin, and `frame-ancestors` replaces it in every current browser.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors https://dennisgr7.dev; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  Link: </llms.txt>; rel="llms-txt"

# Version URLs (previews of non-production branches) are never indexed.
https://:version.:subdomain.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
